      "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vaa-lfAN3hI/mqdefault.jpg",
      "description": "For these tiny turtles, the sea has never felt so far away 🐢😨 \n\nAfter 60 days beneath the sand, these tiny green turtle hatchlings emerge into a world filled with dangers their ancestors never faced. With the ocean just metres away, an unexpected challenge stands between them and their new life.\n\nBlue Planet III: Sir David Attenborough returns 25 years after the original series transformed audiences’ understanding of life beneath the waves. He takes us deeper into our oceans than ever before, revealing extraordinary new stories - filmed using cutting-edge technology.\nAcross six episodes, viewers will journey through five key underwater habitats: Tropical Seas, Open Ocean, Seasonal Seas, Polar Waters, and the Deep, before a final episode looking towards the future of the world's oceans and what can be done to protect them. Made in partnership with The Open University 👉 https://connect.open.ac.uk/ .\n\n#DavidAttenborough #BluePlanet3 #Ocean #Turtles #Sea\n\nSubscribe and 🔔 to the BBC 👉 https://bit.ly/BBCYouTubeSub\nWatch the BBC first on iPlayer 👉 https://bbc.in/iPlayer-Home",
